# Detection

> *Detection engineering transforms observed attacker behavior into repeatable, automated security alerts.*

---

# Overview

Detection engineering is the process of designing, developing, and maintaining analytics that identify malicious or suspicious activity within an environment. In Microsoft Sentinel, detections are implemented as Analytics Rules that continuously evaluate telemetry and generate alerts when predefined conditions are met.

Unlike threat hunting, which is analyst-driven and exploratory, detection engineering automates the identification of known attack patterns, allowing security teams to respond more quickly and consistently.

This section demonstrates how threat hunting queries can be refined into production-ready detections for SSH authentication attacks.

---

# Objectives

The detection queries in this handbook are designed to:

- Detect brute-force authentication attempts
- Identify high-risk source IP addresses
- Reduce false positives
- Generate actionable alerts
- Support incident response workflows

