# Detection 2 — High-Risk Source IP

## Purpose

Identify external IP addresses generating excessive authentication failures.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed password"
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from ([0-9.]+)",1,RawData)
| summarize FailedAttempts=count() by SourceIP
| where FailedAttempts > 20
```

### Why It Matters

A significantly higher number of failures than normal often indicates automated attack activity.

---

# Detection 3 — Authentication Spike

## Purpose

Detect sudden increases in authentication failures over time.

### Query

```kusto
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed password"
| summarize FailedAttempts=count() by bin(TimeGenerated,15m)
| where FailedAttempts > 25
```

### Why It Matters

Sharp spikes in authentication activity frequently indicate scanning or password-spraying campaigns.

---

# Detection 4 — Successful Login After Multiple Failures

## Purpose

Identify accounts that successfully authenticate after several failed login attempts.

### Query

```kusto
let FailedIPs =
MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Failed password"
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from ([0-9.]+)",1,RawData)
| summarize FailedAttempts=count() by SourceIP
| where FailedAttempts >= 5;

MeridianLogs_CL
| where RawData has "Accepted password"
| extend SourceIP = extract(@"from ([0-9.]+)",1,RawData)
| join kind=inner FailedIPs on SourceIP
```

### Why It Matters

A successful login following repeated failures may indicate compromised credentials.

